  'tshwane-police-440-arrests-2026-11-09',
  'Tshwane police arrest 440 people in weekend crime blitz',
  'Community', '2026-11-09', 'SAnews', 'https://www.sanews.gov.za/south-africa/police-arrest-more-400-suspects-tshwane',
  'SAPS-led operations across six Tshwane precincts over the weekend of 7-8 November led to 440 arrests, including suspects wanted for murder and rape.',
  'A joint policing operation across six precincts in the Tshwane District resulted in 440 arrests over the weekend of 7 and 8 November, the South African Police Service said. The operation covered policing precincts in Mamelodi and Sunnyside in the east, Atteridgeville further west, and Temba, Hammanskraal and Ga-Rankuwa to the north, bringing together SAPS units, the Tshwane Metropolitan Police Department, the Department of Home Affairs and local community policing forums.

Detectives had been tracing wanted suspects since the Friday evening before the operation and arrested 242 of them over the weekend. Among this group were two people sought on murder charges, four suspected of kidnapping, four linked to armed robbery, two accused of rape, and 70 implicated in gender-based violence cases. A further 47 people without valid documentation were detained and handed to immigration officials, while 16 motorists were arrested for driving under the influence, 63 people for drinking in public, 11 for drug possession or dealing and one for illegal gambling.

Visible policing during the weekend included roadblocks and stop-and-search checks that covered 985 people and 394 vehicles, with 14 vehicles checked against the stolen vehicle register. Police confiscated 75 small bags containing assorted drugs, along with seven quarter-tablets of the drug Mandrax, plus an undisclosed sum of cash.

A separate liquor compliance sweep checked 57 outlets across the district. Officers closed 25 of them and issued fines to 24 others for breaching the Liquor Act, and confiscated 1,467,280 ml of liquor in the process.

Tshwane District Commissioner Major General Samuel Thine, who led the operation, said the results reflected sustained cooperation between police, metro officers and residents, and that similar high-visibility operations would continue across the district.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.sanews.gov.za/south-africa/police-arrest-more-400-suspects-tshwane", "https://www.citizen.co.za/rekord/news-headlines/2026/11/09/police-arrest-440-suspects-in-tshwane-crime-blitz/"]',
  'agent'
